A 401(k) lets you save nearly 50% more each year than a SIMPLE IRA, giving workers much higher annual contribution limits. Under a SIMPLE IRA, the employer must contribute every year, normally a match of up to 3% of pay or 2% of pay for every eligible employee. Headcount also sets them apart, because a SIMPLE IRA is limited to businesses with 100 or fewer employees while a 401(k) works for any company size.